msgid "Why 1.0 Matters"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"I am pleased to announce the release of https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-"
"java/releases/tag/v1.0.0.Alpha1[A2A Java SDK 1.0.0.Alpha1]. This release "
"represents a significant milestone as we align with the upcoming 1.0 version "
"of the https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A[Agent2Agent (A2A) Protocol "
"specification]. Note that the specification itself is still being finalised, "
"so there might be some subtle changes until the final 1.0 version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The A2A Protocol enables standardized communication between AI agents, "
"allowing them to discover capabilities, delegate tasks, and collaborate "
"seamlessly. This SDK provides a robust Java implementation for building both "
"agents and clients that participate in the A2A ecosystem."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The move to version 1.0 of the A2A specification marks its transition from "
"experimental to production-ready. As the specification matures, we've taken "
"the opportunity to clean up technical debt, modernize our implementation, "
"and establish patterns that will serve us well into the future."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*This release contains breaking changes.* We made the deliberate decision "
"not to maintain backward compatibility with the 0.3.x series, as 1.0 "
"represents the first \"proper\" release of the specification. This allows us "
"to build on a solid foundation without carrying forward legacy patterns."
msgstr ""

msgid "Major Changes"
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Specification Alignment"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The SDK now implements protocol version `1.0` and aligns with the latest "
"https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/blob/main/specification/a2a.proto[a2a."
"proto] definitions. Key specification changes include:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*AgentCard evolution*: The `AgentCard` now uses a `supportedInterfaces` list "
"instead of separate `url`, `preferredTransport`, and `additionalInterfaces` "
"fields. This provides a cleaner, more flexible way to advertise multiple "
"protocol bindings."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Removed kind discriminators*: The 1.0 specification eliminates the `kind` "
"field as a type discriminator, simplifying the protocol."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Refined error handling*: Error classes have been reworked to match the 1.0 "
"specification's error model."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Modern Java: Standardized on Records"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The entire `spec` module has been modernized to use Java records "
"consistently. Previously, we had a mix of traditional classes and records "
"across our domain model. Now all domain classes leverage records for "
"immutability and conciseness, and all getters follow the same naming pattern:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This standardization eliminates confusion and reduces boilerplate while "
"providing a cleaner, more maintainable API."
msgstr ""

msgid "Builder Pattern with Static Factory Methods"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All builders now use static factory methods instead of public constructors. "
"This provides better encapsulation and follows modern Java best practices:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`AgentCard.builder()` creates the builder - constructor is now private"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested builders also use static factory methods"
msgstr ""

msgid "All spec classes follow this pattern consistently"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Builder constructors are now private in the declaring classes, enforcing the "
"use of the static factory method pattern throughout the SDK."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Protocol Buffers as Source of Truth"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We've eliminated our dependency on Jackson and established protocol buffers "
"(protobuf) as the authoritative source for our domain model. The "
"architecture is straightforward:"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Protobuf definitions* in `a2a.proto` define the wire format"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Java records* in the `spec` module provide the SDK's API"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*MapStruct mappers* handle conversions, giving compile errors if protobuf "
"and spec classes go out of sync"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Gson* handles JSON serialization for JSON-RPC transport"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This provides type safety across all transports, a single source of truth "
"for the protocol, and clean separation between wire format and API without "
"cluttering domain classes with serialization annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid "4. Bill of Materials (BOMs)"
msgstr ""

msgid "We've introduced Maven BOMs to simplify dependency management:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Three BOMs are available:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`a2a-java-sdk-bom`: Core SDK and client libraries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`a2a-java-extras-bom`: Optional extensions (JpaDatabaseTaskStore and -"
"PushNotificationStore, replicated QueueManager, Vert.X HTTP client)"
msgstr ""

msgid "`a2a-java-reference-bom`: Quarkus reference implementations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This eliminates version management headaches when using multiple SDK "
"modules, and their dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid "5. Enhanced API Documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every class in the `spec` module now has comprehensive Javadoc explaining "
"its purpose, usage, and relationship to the A2A specification. We've also "
"added detailed documentation for integration points in `server-common` and "
"all client modules."
msgstr ""

msgid "6. Additional Improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Pagination support*: The `ListTasks` and push notification configuration "
"endpoints now support pagination with proper `Result` wrappers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Pluggable HTTP client*: A new `A2AHttpClient` interface allows custom HTTP "
"implementations, with a Vert.x-based implementation provided"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Better validation*: Enhanced input validation across all transports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*TCK progress*: Continuous work towards full compliance with the 1.0 Test "
"Compatibility Kit. The TCK is also work in progress, while the specification "
"is being finalised."
msgstr ""

msgid "Breaking Changes Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you're migrating from 0.3.x, here are the key breaking changes:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*AgentCard structure*: Replace `url` + `preferredTransport` with "
"`supportedInterfaces` list"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Builder pattern*: Use `AgentCard.builder()` instead of `new AgentCard."
"Builder()` - applies to all spec classes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Protocol version*: Update to `AgentCard.CURRENT_PROTOCOL_VERSION` (now `\"1."
"0\"`)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Field renames*: `supportsAuthenticatedExtendedCard` → "
"`supportsExtendedAgentCard`"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Getter naming*: Records use `card.name()` instead of `card.getName()`"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Package cleanup*: The `io.a2a.apec` package has been trimmed"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Serialization*: If you relied on Jackson annotations, migrate to Gson "
"patterns"
msgstr ""

msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

msgid "Using Maven, add the BOM and dependencies:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Creating an agent requires producing an `AgentCard` and an `AgentExecutor`. "
"The `@PublicAgentCard` qualifier marks the public agent card that serves as "
"the entry point for discovery - this is what clients retrieve when "
"discovering your agent. You can also provide an extended agent card with "
"additional authenticated information. Here's a minimal example:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For complete examples, see the https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-java/tree/"
"main/examples/helloworld[Hello World example] in the repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "Looking Forward"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This alpha release brings us significantly closer to a stable 1.0 SDK. Our "
"focus areas for upcoming releases include:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Full compliance with the 1.0 TCK test suite"
msgstr ""

msgid "Performance optimizations based on real-world usage"
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional examples and integration guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "WildFly Feature Pack for seamless Jakarta EE integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The A2A specification itself is still evolving toward its 1.0 release. We're "
"actively participating in the specification process and will continue "
"aligning the SDK as the spec finalizes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Get Involved"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We welcome contributions, feedback, and real-world usage reports! If you're "
"building AI agents or want to explore multi-agent architectures, the A2A "
"Java SDK provides a solid foundation."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Repository*: https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-java"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Examples*: https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-java/tree/main/examples"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Specification*: https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Issues*: https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-java/issues"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Try out 1.0.0.Alpha1 and let us know how it works for your agent use cases!"
msgstr ""
